 of injuries so studies have shown that some red light running cameras will reduce all injury crashes by approximately 20 percent and up to 30 percent for right angle crashes so this is has been proven to be effective in reducing crashes it also has been known to have a spillover effect so this ordinance is requesting installation of cameras at five intersections within the city but once a program has been implemented often there is a reduction in red light running in general throughout the area so the locations in THIS ORDINANCE ARE LISTED ON THE SECOND PAGE OF THE ORDINANCE BUT THEY INCLUDE KING STREET AND LIME KING AND WATER COLUMBIA AVENUE AND WEST END AVENUE LIME AND WALNUT AND THEN MANOR HERSHEY AND WEST END AND THESE LOCATIONS WERE SELECTED BASED ON THE HIGHEST NUMBER OF CRASHES CONTRIBUTED TO RED LIGHT RUNNING WE ALSO TRIED TO DISPERSED THEM THROUGHOUT THE CITY SO NOT focusing on any one particular area and then we've also had some initial coordination with pendot who has to approve the locations that we choose as well so just to provide a little bit more information the program would include and a lot of the details of the program are listed out in the ordinance but the program does include you know required education and signage associated WITH THE CAMERAS AND ALSO INCLUDES A 60 DAY INITIAL PERIOD WHERE VIOLATIONS ARE NOT ISSUED IT'S MORE WARNINGS SO THERE'S PLENTY OF PUBLIC NOTICE ABOUT THE PROGRAM THE TICKETS WILL BE CIVIL OFFENSES THEY ARE NOT CONSIDERED CRIMINAL THEY DO NOT ADD POINTS TO ANYONE'S RECORD THE CITY WILL HAVE TO SET UP SINCE IT IS A CIVIL CIVIL VIOLATION. THE CITY WILL HAVE TO SET UP AN APPEAL PROCESS FOR THOSE CIVIL VIOLATIONS, BUT THAT IS PART OF WHAT WE PLAN TO DO. AND THE SYSTEM WILL NOT GENERATE ANY REVENUE FOR THE CITY. FINES ARE COLLECTED AND THE CITY IS REIMBURSED FOR THEIR EXPENSES RELATED TO THE POLICE TIME AS WELL AS THE VENDOR IS REIMBURSED FOR THOSE EXPENSES. ANY ADDITIONAL REVENUE OVER THAT WOULD GO BACK TO THE STATE. A LOT OF THIS FUNDING THAT GOES BACK TO THE STATE IS USED FOR AUTOMATED RED LIGHT ENFORCEMENT GRANTS, WHICH THE CITY IS OFTEN A RECIPIENT OF AS WELL. SO THE CITY WOULD NOT BE ABLE TO MAKE ANY REVENUE RELATED TO THIS PROGRAM. AND WE'RE ALSO REQUIRED, IF THIS PROGRAM IS IMPLEMENTED, WE WOULD IMPLEMENTED, WE WOULD BE REQUIRED TO DO ANNUAL REPORTS NOTING THE NUMBER OF VIOLATIONS AND DETAILING OUT REVENUE AND EXPENSES RELATED TO THE PROGRAM. SO IF THIS IS APPROVED, THE NEXT STEPS WOULD BE TO MAKE A FORMAL REQUEST, AND THEN BECAUSE THIS HAS TO BE APPROVED BY THE SECRETARY OF TRANSPORTATION, AND THEN WE WOULD ISSUE AN RFP FOR VENDORS.

